{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Now I know.</b> I had knowledge of Him beforehand, and now — even more." "<b>Greater than all the elohim.</b> This teaches that he was familiar with every idolatry in the world — for he left no idol that he did not worship (Mekhilta)." "<b>For by the plan that they schemed against them.</b> As its Targum renders — with water they plotted to destroy them, and they were destroyed in the water." "<b>That they schemed.</b> That they acted wickedly. And our Sages interpreted it as the language of ״וַיָּזֶד יַעֲקֹב נָזִיד״ — in the pot in which they cooked, they were cooked (Sotah 11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:57.391971635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}